course: dictionary
lesson: 7440
title: Polygraph: a machine that measures nervousness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A polygraph is a machine that measures a person's breathing, heartbeat, blood pressure and sweating while they answer questions. People often call it a «lie detector», but it measures what the body does, not the truth itself.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «Lie-detector machines (polygraphs) measure nervousness, like heartbeat and sweat, and honest people get nervous too, so they are not reliable.» The brackets tell you that polygraphs and lie-detector machines are the same thing. The sentence says the machine measures nervousness, and honest people can be nervous too, so it can make mistakes.
explain: Look for the word that tells you what kind of word it is. A polygraph is a machine, but a polygraph test is the questioning done with that machine. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «The polygraph measured her heartbeat and sweat while she answered» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A polygraph is a machine that measures breathing, heartbeat, blood pressure and sweating.
fact: A polygraph is often called a «lie detector».
fact: A polygraph test is the questioning done with the machine.
fact: A polygraph measures nervousness in the body, not lies themselves, so it can make mistakes.
fact: Useful phrases are «take a polygraph test», «pass the polygraph» and «lie detector».
exercise: «Lie-detector machines (polygraphs) measure nervousness.» What does a polygraph measure? | The weight and height of a person | *Breathing, heartbeat, blood pressure and sweating | The colour of the clothes they wear | Thoughts and dreams
exercise: Ella says a polygraph always finds liars for sure. Why might she be wrong? | Nervous honest people can get the same body signs as liars | It is only a clock that ticks | *It measures nervousness, and honest people can also be nervous, so it can make mistakes | Polygraphs only work on animals
exercise: What is a polygraph test? | *The questioning done with a polygraph machine | A school test about spelling | A medical check of the eyes | A race between two machines
test: Which word is another name for a polygraph? | *Lie detector | Calculator | Telescope | Thermometer
test: Which of these phrases means succeeding on a polygraph? | Break the polygraph | *Pass the polygraph | Forget the polygraph | Lose the polygraph
exam: Why does the polygraph «measure nervousness, like heartbeat and sweat» rather than lies themselves? | *Because nervousness is what the body shows, and the machine cannot read the truth directly | Because it is a weather instrument | Because the machine can read minds | Because lies make people sneeze
